  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Facilitating Regular Pathways for Regular Migration and Socioeconomic Integration in Support of Uruguayan Migration Commitments</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program aims to implement Community Sponsorship in Uruguay by strengthening the knowledge and capacities of government institutions, civil society, the private sector and host communities, while working in two lines of action: Institutional strengthening to reinforce the regularization pathways; and promoting the socio-economic integration of migrants and refugees to grow in a sustainable way in the country. The programme goal is to prepare host communities for reception, which will be conducted through quality prepared programmes for refugees and receiving communities that are co-designed and implemented in collaboration with local authorities, refugees and diaspora. Such programmes allow refugees not only to demonstrate the skills and aptitudes they have, but also to contribute to the communities that have welcomed them.  In this way, IOM will link the needs of the country with the development potential of migration, involving the receiving community in the process, taking their opinion into account and empowering civil society to be a bridge on this path.</narrative>
  </description>
